@ans Tenth
@end

@table
Health scheme | Year | Key point
**National Health Policy** | **1983**, 2002, **2017** | 2017: public health spending **2.5% of GDP** by 2025
**National Rural Health Mission** | **12 April 2005** (Tenth Plan) | Village health worker **ASHA**; merged with the urban mission into the **National Health Mission** (2013)
**Rashtriya Swasthya Bima Yojana** | 2008 | Health cover for **unorganised sector** BPL workers, under the Unorganised Workers' Social Security Act 2008
**Ayushman Bharat PM-JAY** | **23 September 2018** | **Rs. 5 lakh per family** (not per person) a year; Centre-State **60:40** (90:10 in the north-east and Himalayan states); since 2024 all people **70+** are covered
PM Ayushman Bharat Health Infrastructure Mission | 2021 | Health infrastructure (Budget 2021-22)
@end

@q 10:8-10

India's public health spending was about **1.1% of GDP** in 2009-10 and is under **2%** now. Life expectancy at birth is about **70 years**, a little higher for women than men.

