@q 10:132-140

**Bonded labour** was abolished by ordinance in **1975** (Act 1976). **CAPART** (1986, Ministry of Rural Development) funds voluntary rural development work. **Aadhaar** (UIDAI) is a 12-digit identity number; the first was given at **Tembhli** (Nandurbar, Maharashtra) on 29 September 2010. **PURA** came from **A.P.J. Abdul Kalam**. The first open university was **Andhra Pradesh Open University** (Hyderabad, 1982), now Dr. B.R. Ambedkar Open University. **Tarun Bharat Sangh** (Rajendra Singh, "Waterman of India") works in **Rajasthan**.

@up UP link: UP ran the **School Chalo Abhiyan** (2000), the **Kalp Yojana** (primary education) and the **Shiksha Mitra** scheme (2000) to fill teacher gaps with local youth. UP has among the most **Ayushman card** holders, and the **Kasturba Gandhi Balika Vidyalayas** are run in every block.

@trap
**NRHM 12 April 2005 (Tenth Plan); ASHA.** **ICDS 1975; blindness programme 1976; leprosy 1983.** **PM-JAY: Rs. 5 lakh per family, 60:40.** **Skill India 15 July 2015.** **STRIDE is not a skill scheme.** **Global Skill Park: Bhopal.** **AIM: NITI Aayog.** **BBBP 22 January 2015.** **Swadhar = women in difficulty.** **Swavalambini 2025 = MSDE, north-east.** **JSY replaced National Maternity Benefit Scheme.** **PMSBY Rs. 20, 18-70; PMJJBY Rs. 436.** **NSAP 1995.** **Operation Blackboard 1987 → NLM 1988 → SSA 2001 → Saakshar Bharat 2009.** **Mid-day Meal 1995 → PM POSHAN 2021.** **National Children's Fund 1979.**
@end

@heatmap

@pattern
Scheme-year matches dominate: the **2019-2025** papers asked at least two each year (health, insurance, skill, education). Recent papers also ask **contribution amounts** (PMJJBY, PMSBY, APY) and the ministry behind a scheme.
@end

@next
Likely next angles: **Ayushman Vay Vandana** cards for 70+, **U-WIN** immunisation, **POSHAN 2.0**, **PM-SHRI** schools, **NEP 2020** structure (5+3+3+4), **APAAR ID**, **PM Vishwakarma**, **Lakhpati Didi** (3 crore target) and **e-Shram** registration.
@end
